# React + Inertia Conventions (Implementation Layer)

**Scope:** React 19 + Inertia 3 + Tailwind 4 + TypeScript implementation only.  
**UX principles (framework-independent):** `02-ui-ux.mdc`, `UI-CONTRACT.md`, `COLOR-TYPOGRAPHY-GOVERNANCE.md`

Reference: `.cursor/architecture/api-conventions.md`

## Stack
React 19 + Inertia 3 + Tailwind 4 + Radix UI + TypeScript

## Directory Structure
```
resources/js/
├── components/     # Reusable UI (ui/ = Radix primitives)
├── hooks/
├── layouts/        # app-layout, auth-layout, settings
├── pages/          # Inertia pages mirror routes
│   ├── attendance/
│   ├── enrollment/
│   └── reports/
├── types/
└── lib/utils.ts
```

## Page Rules
- One page component per route in `pages/{module}/`
- Use `AppLayout` for authenticated pages
- Receive props from controller — no direct API fetch in pages unless polling
- Required UI states (`idle`, `loading`, `success`, `empty`, `error`, `disabled`, `retry`) — see `02-ui-ux.mdc`

## Forms
```tsx
// ✅ useForm from Inertia
const { data, setData, post, processing, errors } = useForm({ records: [] });
post(route('attendance.batch', sectionId));
```

## Permissions
```tsx
// Check permissions from shared auth prop
{auth.permissions.includes('attendance.write') && (
  <Button onClick={submit}>حفظ الحضور</Button>
)}
```

## RTL & Arabic — Required from Day One
- `dir="rtl"` on root layout when locale is `ar`
- Use logical properties: `ms-`, `me-`, `ps-`, `pe-` (not ml/mr)
- Numbers: `<span dir="ltr">{studentCode}</span>` inside RTL context
- All user-facing strings via Laravel `__()` / JSON lang files — no hardcoded Arabic in components except prototypes

## Tables (45K scale)
- Server-side pagination only — never load 45K rows client-side
- Use cursor pagination from backend
- Virtual scrolling for lists > 100 rows if client-side slice needed

## Attendance Batch UI
- Submit 50 students as single batch POST
- Show `processing` while queue job runs (poll or Inertia reload)
- Display `last_updated_at` on dashboard widgets

## Notifications
- Use `sonner` toast for flash messages
- Success/error from Inertia `usePage().props.flash`

## Accessibility
- Radix components for keyboard navigation
- Label all form inputs
- Focus management in modals (Dialog)
- Broader a11y requirements: `02-ui-ux.mdc`

## Forbidden
- `fetch()` to internal API bypassing Inertia for CRUD
- Business logic in page components — keep in hooks or utils
- Inline styles — Tailwind only
- English-only UI strings in production pages
